<article class="env-exercise" id="02CI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02CI">Exercise <span data-tag="02CI">111.1.3</span>.</a> Suppose that $(A, {\mathfrak m}, k)$ is a Noetherian local ring. For any finite $A$-module $M$ define $r(M)$ to be the minimum number of generators of $M$ as an $A$-module. This number equals $\dim _ k M/{\mathfrak m} M = \dim _ k M \otimes _ A k$ by NAK. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Show that $r(M \otimes _ A N) = r(M)r(N)$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Let $I\subset A $ be an ideal with $r(I) > 1$. Show that $r(I^2) < r(I)^2$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Conclude that if every ideal in $A$ is a flat module, then $A$ is a PID (or a field). 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>